$DIR/test.p:5:13: use of untyped nil in argument to new
    nil has no type of its own: it is the zero value of pointers, slices,
    interfaces and func values. A variable declared with := or var and no type
    takes the type of its value, and nil gives it none. Write the type.
    (see "Variable declarations" in the Plutonium spec, section 10.10)
    (run "pluto explain E0016" for a longer explanation)
